{"id": "sim4-s4-W25-0034-1", "decision": "fix_clean", "clean": "Here are the directions to our place, because the GPS always gets it wrong. You take exit 42, not 43, off the highway and turn left at the gas station, then go about a mile and a half until you see a red barn on your right. Don't turn there. Keep going until the road curves and there's a mailbox shaped like a fish. That's us, number 207. The driveway is gravel and kind of steep, so take it slow. There's room to park by the oak tree, and if you get lost just call me. My cell is 555-0142. I'll be in the garden probably. Dinner's at 6, but come earlier if you want to see the chickens. They're the main attraction, I'm not joking.", "reason": "homophone", "note": "There->They're"}
